# Chorus as published in 1927 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats; "Oh! we" is the pickup)
Oh! we ain't got a bar-rel of mon-ey,
Eb4/. F4// G4 G4/. Ab4// G4/. F#4// G4 Ab4(2) G4(2)
may-be we're rag-ged and fun-ny,
Bb4 Bb4/. Bb4// Bb4/. A4// Bb4 C5(2) Bb4
but we'll trav-el a-long, sing-in' a song,
Bb4/. B4// C5/. B4// C5/ Eb5/ ~Eb5(2) G4/ Ab4/ A4/ Bb4/ ~Bb4(2)
side by side.
Eb4(2) F4(2) Eb4(4)
Don't know what's com-in' to-mor-row,
G4 G4/. Ab4// G4/. F#4// G4 Ab4(2) G4(2)
may-be it's trou-ble and sor-row,
Bb4 Bb4/. Bb4// Bb4/. A4// Bb4 C5(2) Bb4
but we'll trav-el the road, sha-rin' our load
Bb4/. B4// C5/. B4// C5/ Eb5/ ~Eb5(2) G4/ Ab4/ A4/ Bb4/ ~Bb4(2)
side by side.
Eb4(2) F4(2) Eb4(4)
